// The query-suffix half of cratestack#802's collision, sibling to
// `tanstack_mutation_hook_collision.cstack`. Model `Post` derives
// `usePostListQuery` from `{% if model.allows_list %}`
// (`templates/src/rest-react-query.ts.j2:31`), and the bare (i.e. query)
// `procedure post_list` derives the same identifier: `to_pascal_case("post_list")`
// is `PostList`, so the hook is `usePostListQuery`.
//
// Deliberately `post_list` and NOT `list_posts`, which would be `model
// Post`'s own generated axum handler `handle_list_posts` and so is
// rejected by `cratestack-parser`'s `validate::procedure_handler_collisions`
// (cratestack#784) before this generator ever sees the schema. The
// tokenizer treats the two as distinct word sequences — [post, list] vs
// [list, posts] — which is exactly what lets this one through the parser
// and into the generator where the hook-name collision actually lives.
//
// Both files exist because the check has two entry points, one per hook
// suffix, and a single fixture can only ever prove the first error the
// check returns.

datasource db {
  provider = "postgresql"
  url = env("DATABASE_URL")
}

auth SessionUser {
  id Int
}

model Post {
  id Int @id
  title String

  @@allow("read", true)
}

procedure post_list(): Post
  @allow(auth() != null)
